+++</md></sn><sn><md>### Modem

**Modem** stands for **Modulator-Demodulator**.

Computer only reads digital signals whereas the internet only reads analog signals.So a device or system is require to handle this data conversion.

A modem converts signals between the form used by a local network/device and the form required by the communication system of an ISP or other access network.

![img](https://data-flair.training/blogs/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2021/12/how-does-a-modem-work.webp)

```text
Your Network  → Switch/Hub →  Router →  Modem  →  ISP Network  →  Internet
```

**Main function:**

* Performs the necessary `signal conversion` for a particular Internet access technology.
* The exact signaling depends on the access technology(Cable / DSL / Fiber access).

**Important:** A modem and router are not inherently the same thing. Many home devices combine a modem, router, switch, Wi-Fi access point, and other functions into one box.


